# Xplorer ENGINEERING / DEV build.
#
# Identical to CubeOrangePlus-ODID except that the @READONLY markers in
# defaults.parm are ignored for the subsystems listed in
# libraries/AP_Param/xplorer_dev_unlock.h, and the GCS_Param_Clamps.h hard
# clamp table is bypassed. This exists so engineering can tune PSC / ATC / EK3
# and the filters over MAVLink without a firmware rebuild per change.
#
# NOT FOR CUSTOMER AIRCRAFT.
#
# BOARD ID: deliberately inherited from CubeOrangePlus-ODID (10163), NOT unique.
# Fielded Xplorer bootloaders are built with AP_SIGNED_FIRMWARE and enforce
# APJ_BOARD_ID == 10163 with no ALT_BOARD_ID, so a firmware carrying any other
# board ID simply cannot be uploaded to an existing aircraft. A unique ID would
# make this build undeployable rather than safer.
#
# That means separation here is PROCEDURAL, not hardware-enforced:
#   - the boot banner reports "DEV BUILD - NOT FOR PRODUCTION" at WARNING severity
#   - the build output lives under build/CubeOrangePlus-ODID-DEV/
#   - DEV apj files must never be published to the release/update channel
# This build still has to be signed with the Arcsky key to boot, so treat a
# signed DEV apj with the same care as a production one.
#
# For hardware-enforced separation you would give dev airframes a bootloader
# carrying a SECOND signing key (make_secure_bl.py takes up to 10) and sign DEV
# firmware with that key only. Production bootloaders, holding just the
# production key, would then reject DEV firmware outright. That needs a
# one-time bootloader flash per dev airframe - see Tools/xplorer/README.md.
#
# Build:
#   ./waf configure --board CubeOrangePlus-ODID-DEV
#   ./waf copter
#
# defaults.parm in this directory is a byte-identical copy of the ODID one.
# It has to be a copy because chibios_hwdef.py only looks for defaults.parm in
# the board's own directory, not through the include chain. The unlock is done
# at runtime by parameter name, so the two files never need to differ -
# gen_param_docs.py fails if they drift.

include ../CubeOrangePlus-ODID/hwdef.dat

# APJ_BOARD_ID is intentionally NOT overridden - we inherit 10163 from
# CubeOrangePlus-ODID so this firmware is uploadable to existing aircraft.
# See the note above before changing it.

# Embed the production ODID bootloader rather than expecting a
# Tools/bootloaders/CubeOrangePlus-ODID-DEV_bl.bin that does not exist. Correct
# because this target is the same hardware and the same board ID (10163); it
# also means there is no DEV bootloader to build, sign or accidentally flash.
USE_BOOTLOADER_FROM_BOARD CubeOrangePlus-ODID

# Ignore @READONLY for the dev unlock list, and bypass the clamp table.
define XPLORER_DEV_UNLOCK_ENABLED 1
